---
/**
 * Privacy policy — required once the site processes any personal data
 * (UK GDPR + Data Protection Act 2018), which it does via WhatsApp/phone
 * enquiries and the third-party requests listed below.
 *
 * Kept to what's actually verifiable — the registered company details below
 * are confirmed against Companies House (company 16013011). Still no claims
 * about ICO registration, a VAT number, or a dedicated privacy contact,
 * since none of those are confirmed. Before this goes live, Mumthaz should:
 *   1. Confirm whether the company is registered with the ICO (data
 *      protection fee) and, if so, add the registration reference below.
 *   2. Decide on a contact route for privacy/data requests specifically —
 *      currently this points people at the phone/WhatsApp numbers already
 *      in src/config/site.ts, since no email address is configured anywhere
 *      on the site.
 *   3. Confirm how long customer/vehicle records are actually kept (the
 *      retention section below uses a deliberately generic answer).
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site, address, phones, legal, url } from '../config/site';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Toyotech MOT Centre"
  description="How Toyotech MOT Centre in Bletchley, Milton Keynes handles personal data collected through this website, WhatsApp and phone enquiries."
>
  <section class="bg-navy text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-black">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/80">
        This page explains what personal data {site.name} collects through this website and when you contact us,
        why, and what your rights are. Last updated {lastUpdated}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-navy">Who we are</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">
        {site.name} ({site.altName}) is a trading name of {legal.companyName}, a company registered in{' '}
        {legal.jurisdiction}, company no. {legal.companyNumber}. We are the data controller for the personal data
        described on this page. Our registered office and workshop address is {legal.registeredOffice}. You can
        reach us by phone or WhatsApp — see the numbers at the bottom of this page or on our{' '}
        <a class="font-semibold text-brand-blue underline underline-offset-4" href={url('/contact')}>Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-navy">The personal data we collect</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">This website is a static, no-login brochure site. We don't run a booking
        form, a user account system, or a payment system — so almost everything below only happens if you choose
        to contact us.</p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-bold text-navy">When you message or call us</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">
        If you message us on WhatsApp or call one of our numbers, we see your phone number, your name if you give
        it, and whatever you tell us about your vehicle or booking. We use this to reply to you, arrange your MOT
        or repair, and keep basic records of the work.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-bold text-navy">Automatically, from visiting this website</h3>
      <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-2 text-slate-700">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-navy">Site analytics.</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookieless —
          it doesn't use any tracking script or device identifier and doesn't build a profile of you. It gives us
          aggregate figures like page views, not who you are.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-navy">Opening hours.</strong> Your browser fetches our current opening hours from a
          Google Sheet published by us. This is a request from your browser to Google's servers, so Google
          receives your IP address as part of that request, the same as loading any web page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-navy">Map.</strong> The map on our Home and Contact pages uses OpenFreeMap, a free,
          open map data service — it doesn't use cookies or tracking, though the map tile requests do go to
          OpenFreeMap's servers, the same as any image loaded from another website.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-bold text-navy">If you click through to another site</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">
        The WhatsApp button, the "Get directions" link and our Google reviews link all take you to a different
        website when you click them — WhatsApp/Meta or Google. Once you're there, it's covered by their privacy
        policy, not ours, and it's your choice whether to click through.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-navy">Cookies</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">
        This website does not set any cookies of its own, and none of the third-party services it uses (Cloudflare
        Analytics, the opening-hours sheet, or the map) set cookies on your browser either. If that ever changes —
        for example if we add a live chat widget or a different analytics tool — we'll update this page and add a
        cookie banner if one becomes necessary.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-navy">Why we're allowed to use it</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">
        When you contact us about a booking or repair, we use your details because you've asked us to take a
        specific action — arranging a service — which is our <em>legitimate interest</em> in running the
        business and, once you book, is necessary to carry out that job. For the cookieless analytics described
        above, our legitimate interest is understanding how the website is used, weighed against the minimal,
        non-identifying nature of that data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-navy">Who we share it with</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">We don't sell or rent your personal data. It's only shared where the service
        itself requires it:</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2 text-slate-700">
        <li><strong class="text-navy">Meta / WhatsApp</strong> — carries the messages if you contact us that way.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-navy">Cloudflare</strong> — provides the cookieless analytics beacon.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-navy">Google</strong> — hosts the published spreadsheet our opening hours are read from, and the Google Business listing our reviews link out to.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-navy">OpenFreeMap</strong> — serves the map tiles shown on this site.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">
        We don't use any other analytics, advertising or marketing platforms, and we don't share your details with
        anyone for their own marketing purposes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-navy">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">
        We keep enquiry and booking messages for as long as we reasonably need them to deal with your enquiry and
        any follow-up (such as a warranty query). Records connected to work we've invoiced are kept for as long as
        UK tax law requires business records to be retained. We don't keep personal data longer than we need it
        for these purposes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-navy">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Under UK GDPR, you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 text-slate-700 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <li>See the personal data we hold about you</li>
        <li>Correct anything that's inaccurate</li>
        <li>Delete your data, where we don't need to keep it</li>
        <li>Restrict or object to how we use it</li>
        <li>Get a copy in a portable format</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">
        To ask us about any of this, contact us using the numbers below. If you're not satisfied with our
        response, you have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at
        <a class="font-semibold text-brand-blue underline underline-offset-4" href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="nofollow"
          >ico.org.uk</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-navy">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">
        If we change what data we collect or how we use it, we'll update this page and change the date at the
        top.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-navy">Contact us about this policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">{address.full}</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-1 text-slate-700">
        {
          phones.map((p) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`tel:${p.tel}`} class="font-semibold text-brand-blue underline underline-offset-4">{p.display}</a>
              <span class="text-slate-500"> — {p.label}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
